					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sunnyclockwork" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1621343); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1621343&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608670547" alt="SunnyClockwork" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1621343)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sunnyclockwork" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1621343); return false;" >SunnyClockwork</a></span> <span class="odate time_1486395247 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Feb 2017 15:34</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2741351">
									

<p>Well mainly because the thing is in a very delicate situation right now? If -2 were to be neutralized, -K will break free, and Foundation doesn't have a completely safe backup plan in case that happens. And -2 could just be very easily killed so Foundation doesn't want to draw any attention to it.</p>
<p>The fake version is possibly the &quot;public version&quot; on the Foundation database, which aims at misleading people into thinking the monster is already sealed safely in a thousand-meter deep iron lake, and is unlikely to break free just like it has been for thousands of years. The fake version undermines -2's role so that people won't notice and the interview gives just enough info to present yet another vague story.</p>
<p>And in a narrative sense, all the actual Sarkic/CotBG are emphasized in the second version. I was hoping to create a sense of, presenting the conventional vague myth story in the first version, and revealing a much detailed and grounded truth in the second one ._.</p>
<p>Still, it's fair that if you feel like it's repetitive, and thanks for reading.</p>

							</div>

								
					
